__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv*/
venv/
*.env
build/
dist/
.pytest-tmp/
.pytest_cache/
# review/agent-teams scratch (locked by an earlier sandbox token's DACL, so it
# cannot be deleted without admin - ignoring it stops git warning on every
# status while it exists)
.rv-run/
.agent-teams/
app/_version_baked.py
*.spec.bak
# user data / runtime state (SP-04). The rule is "never commit data/" - the
# old file enumerated artefacts (`data/*.db`, `data/*.csv`, ...) and therefore
# missed `data/.export-<hex>.zip` (the spool of a GET /api/export that was
# aborted) and `data/*.db-journal`, both of which hold user data. Ignore the
# whole folder and re-include the one tracked placeholder.
data/
!data/panos/
data/panos/*
!data/panos/.gitkeep
# downloaded catalog inputs (OpenNGC etc.) are regenerable, not repo content:
# scripts/build_adv_catalog.py fetches them, and a stray `git add -A` must not
# commit a multi-MB third-party CSV. Covering `data/` above covers them.
# Popularity tooling: the CACHE is regenerable (fetched), but
# `scripts/match_popularity.py` is TRACKED - it generates the committed
# `app/popularity_data.py`, and a generated data file whose tool is not in the
# repo cannot be regenerated (the old curated POPULARITY table had exactly that
# problem). Only a stray ROOT copy stays ignored.
popularity_snapshot.json
/match_popularity.py
theme-preview/
.dsh-vision-toolkit/
dist/release/
logs/
# browser-gate failure artifacts (screenshots + DOM dumps): regenerable, and a
# failing run must not leave repo noise behind.
tests/browser/artifacts/
# sandbox-created scratch copies inside the review evidence: the DACL on these
# makes them unreadable to the current user, so git cannot even traverse them
# (`git add -A` aborts with "could not open directory"). They are throwaway
# copies of repo files, never evidence.
reviews/*/evidence/scratch/

# DSH AgentTeams harness state (task/mailbox bookkeeping, not repo content)
.agent-teams/

# Requested dated UI captures/mockups remain local review evidence.
/image-catalog-reference/current-ui-*/
/image-catalog-reference/generated-from-current-*/
